# Top-level static-check tools installed from PyPI.
#
# requirements-tools.txt is GENERATED from this file by
# scripts/gen_pip_hashes.sh (uv pip compile --generate-hashes), run inside
# the image's own base (linux/amd64 python:3.12-slim) so the resolution
# matches what the image will actually install.
#
# The generated file is installed with `pip install --require-hashes`, which
# refuses to install anything whose artifact hash is not listed -- and which
# requires the FULL transitive closure to be pinned and hashed. That is the
# standard mechanism for PyPI supply-chain integrity, and it is why this
# cannot be a hand-maintained list of top-level pins.
